1
00:00:00,011 --> 00:00:01,469
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,470 --> 00:00:03,011
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,178 --> 00:00:05,302
(Episode 55)

4
00:00:05,303 --> 00:00:06,845
- Thank you. Goodbye.
- Thank you.

5
00:00:12,136 --> 00:00:14,886
- Mom.
- Yes, Seung Hyun. How is it?

6
00:00:15,886 --> 00:00:17,220
Did you replace it?

7
00:00:17,511 --> 00:00:18,970
Who else would?

8
00:00:19,663 --> 00:00:23,636
I didn't notice when I used it here,
but after sleeping on a nice bed there,

9
00:00:23,678 --> 00:00:25,470
I realized how old mine was.

10
00:00:25,845 --> 00:00:28,345
It had no cushioning,
and it was uncomfortable.

11
00:00:28,970 --> 00:00:31,803
Since Se Ri will use it,
I wanted to buy her one.

12
00:00:38,678 --> 00:00:40,178
Have you thought about it?

13
00:00:43,136 --> 00:00:44,136
Yeah.

14
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:49,512
I have, but I don't want to pretend
to love someone, even if it's fake.

15
00:00:49,970 --> 00:00:53,720
You know how I feel about love.
It makes me uncomfortable right away.

16
00:00:54,178 --> 00:00:58,345
And I don't think pretending to date
just to keep Do Hee away is right, either.

17
00:00:59,928 --> 00:01:01,653
People don't dwell on what others say.

18
00:01:01,654 --> 00:01:02,928
They'll stop talking about it soon.

19
00:01:03,095 --> 00:01:04,220
What if they don't?

20
00:01:04,303 --> 00:01:07,136
Don't. Don't jinx it.

21
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:11,380
You'll get judged every time
you're with Ji Hu, like yesterday.

22
00:01:11,928 --> 00:01:15,011
If people think we're dating,
you'll be protected.

23
00:01:15,345 --> 00:01:16,928
And Ji Hu will feel more at ease too.

24
00:01:18,636 --> 00:01:19,803
Ji Hu...

25
00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:24,970
Don't think you're a burden to me.
Luckily, I don't have a girlfriend.

26
00:01:26,033 --> 00:01:28,720
May I ask why you're going this far?

27
00:01:29,053 --> 00:01:32,392
Because you and Ji Hu seem
so uncomfortable with all this.

28
00:01:33,082 --> 00:01:34,552
Ji Hu is my friend, and you...

29
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:39,814
Ever since I saw you sacrifice yourself
for your nephew, I saw you differently.

30
00:01:40,053 --> 00:01:41,803
I guess, in a way, I respect you.

31
00:01:41,886 --> 00:01:44,264
That's so cheesy.

32
00:01:45,386 --> 00:01:48,165
You did something without hesitation
that I never could have done.

33
00:01:48,382 --> 00:01:49,840
So I want to help you.

34
00:01:50,303 --> 00:01:51,928
Does that answer your question?

35
00:01:52,803 --> 00:01:56,386
Anyway, I want to be your shield.

36
00:02:00,095 --> 00:02:01,186
I understand.

37
00:02:02,011 --> 00:02:03,845
What? So we're a couple starting today?

38
00:02:05,985 --> 00:02:07,027
Yes.

39
00:02:10,301 --> 00:02:12,801
- You're here?
- Aunt, you're here.

40
00:02:12,845 --> 00:02:14,011
Were you waiting for me?

41
00:02:14,345 --> 00:02:16,821
Of course. I guess I've gotten used to it.

42
00:02:16,875 --> 00:02:18,428
The house felt so lonely without you.

43
00:02:18,470 --> 00:02:20,970
Thank you. Come eat.

44
00:02:21,095 --> 00:02:22,136
Okay.

45
00:02:43,178 --> 00:02:44,345
- Yes.
- What are you doing?

46
00:02:46,095 --> 00:02:47,345
Is something wrong?

47
00:02:47,470 --> 00:02:48,687
I'll be right down.

48
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:49,970
Are dad and mom here?

49
00:02:50,136 --> 00:02:52,098
They have plans today.

50
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:53,970
So it's just you and me?

51
00:03:01,901 --> 00:03:03,628
I think I like her.

52
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:05,668
Sounds like it.

53
00:03:06,869 --> 00:03:08,595
Then you should tell her.

54
00:03:09,428 --> 00:03:12,095
I can't. It'll be hard for her.

55
00:03:13,803 --> 00:03:15,595
My friend would be much better for her.

56
00:03:15,928 --> 00:03:17,553
How? How would he be better?

57
00:03:17,678 --> 00:03:19,108
He doesn't have my baggage.

58
00:03:20,058 --> 00:03:22,761
He could make things much easier for her.

59
00:03:23,136 --> 00:03:26,803
I don't think you fall in love
just to make things easier, do you?

60
00:03:27,678 --> 00:03:29,136
I'm complicated.

61
00:03:30,636 --> 00:03:34,136
You've got more baggage than I thought.
You look like a prince.

62
00:03:34,428 --> 00:03:37,316
I'm not a prince. I'm the Little Mermaid.

63
00:03:37,761 --> 00:03:40,470
What? A man who's the Little Mermaid?

64
00:03:41,261 --> 00:03:43,178
She laughed too. She said it was weird.

65
00:03:45,553 --> 00:03:48,920
Who could she be?
I'm getting more curious.

66
00:03:51,678 --> 00:03:53,088
Can I stop eating?

67
00:03:53,963 --> 00:03:56,011
I shouldn't leave food behind.

68
00:03:56,928 --> 00:03:58,720
I'll take care of it. Go upstairs.

69
00:03:58,970 --> 00:04:00,011
Thank you.

70
00:04:13,970 --> 00:04:14,970
Hi.

71
00:04:27,261 --> 00:04:28,303
Why are you laughing?

72
00:04:29,303 --> 00:04:32,803
It's funny to see you unable
to do as you please. So what?

73
00:04:43,470 --> 00:04:45,720
If you have a marker, could I borrow it?

74
00:04:45,970 --> 00:04:49,428
Sure. What do you need it for?

75
00:04:52,386 --> 00:04:55,386
(O Reum's Banh Xeo)

76
00:05:10,386 --> 00:05:11,595
Does it look weird?

77
00:05:11,928 --> 00:05:13,470
Is this a sign?

78
00:05:13,511 --> 00:05:15,220
Yeah. Why?

79
00:05:15,928 --> 00:05:17,179
Want me to draw it for you?

80
00:05:18,595 --> 00:05:20,011
Would you?

81
00:05:21,886 --> 00:05:24,545
I've drawn O Reum a lot before.

82
00:05:24,583 --> 00:05:26,923
Give me a photo, and I'll draw it for you.

83
00:05:27,553 --> 00:05:28,595
Okay.

84
00:05:48,928 --> 00:05:49,970
Here.

85
00:05:54,386 --> 00:05:56,053
I miss him so much.

86
00:05:57,511 --> 00:05:59,244
Your mom told me about the agreement.

87
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:00,734
Thank you.

88
00:06:01,259 --> 00:06:03,642
I'll still thank her properly.

89
00:06:05,386 --> 00:06:07,303
You really don't have to worry about that.

90
00:06:08,470 --> 00:06:10,595
Can I give this to you by tomorrow?

91
00:06:13,470 --> 00:06:15,511
I'm always indebted to you.

92
00:06:18,205 --> 00:06:21,746
I might draw this really badly, you know.

93
00:06:22,011 --> 00:06:23,053
What?

94
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:29,178
Ta-da!

95
00:06:29,970 --> 00:06:31,095
What's this?

96
00:06:31,678 --> 00:06:32,761
Are you trying to pay me off?

97
00:06:32,845 --> 00:06:34,345
It's money, but it's for living expenses.

98
00:06:34,678 --> 00:06:37,011
The cash folded inside is for Sun Kyung,

99
00:06:37,053 --> 00:06:40,294
and you can use the card and the rest
of the cash however you want.

100
00:06:42,761 --> 00:06:44,011
Aren't you touched?

101
00:06:46,553 --> 00:06:49,437
It's been so long
since I got living expenses.

102
00:06:49,514 --> 00:06:50,678
I'm touched.

103
00:06:58,271 --> 00:07:01,263
Now that you're the lady of this house,
I'll give you an allowance every month.

104
00:07:01,678 --> 00:07:02,949
I promised.

105
00:07:03,196 --> 00:07:07,428
I married you because I wanted
to spoil you with nice, expensive things.

106
00:07:19,803 --> 00:07:21,595
- Why...
- Enough.

107
00:07:31,803 --> 00:07:33,011
I like hearing that, Aunt.

108
00:07:33,136 --> 00:07:34,928
Your uncle keeps making me laugh.

109
00:07:38,886 --> 00:07:40,970
- Can you hear us?
- How could I not?

110
00:07:41,386 --> 00:07:43,136
- Buy me earplugs.
- I'm broke.

111
00:07:43,178 --> 00:07:45,595
I heard you say you'd spoil her
with all kinds of nice things.

112
00:07:45,678 --> 00:07:48,053
Exactly. I gave all my money away.
I'm broke.

113
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:54,095
Is Su Yeon coming this week?

114
00:07:55,595 --> 00:07:56,845
She'll be here this week.

115
00:07:58,053 --> 00:08:00,178
You won't have to struggle anymore.

116
00:08:01,595 --> 00:08:02,761
Was it hard for you?

117
00:08:03,928 --> 00:08:07,976
No, it's just that this isn't really
my household to manage,

118
00:08:08,261 --> 00:08:11,220
but I enjoyed getting closer to you.

119
00:08:11,761 --> 00:08:15,678
Su Yeon is my sister-in-law too,
so I'll try to get along with her better.

120
00:08:16,095 --> 00:08:17,595
- Good.
- Yes.

121
00:08:17,761 --> 00:08:20,261
You've suddenly had to deal
with all these in-law duties.

122
00:08:20,296 --> 00:08:23,421
I haven't made her do anything.
What's gotten into you all?

123
00:08:23,636 --> 00:08:27,678
Yes, thanks to that,
I've gotten closer to Joong Bin too.

124
00:08:28,553 --> 00:08:31,803
You didn't forget your lunch plans
today, did you?

125
00:08:32,261 --> 00:08:34,761
- Are you going to meet her?
- How long will Do Hee control him?

126
00:08:34,803 --> 00:08:36,261
He needs to meet someone new.

127
00:08:36,928 --> 00:08:38,011
I'll try.

128
00:08:46,553 --> 00:08:50,636
Joong Bin, if Sun Kyung's feet hurt,
why do you only give her herbal medicine?

129
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:53,595
- What else can I do?
- It's good to give her healthy things,

130
00:08:53,636 --> 00:08:56,678
but what's the point
if she's wearing heels all day?

131
00:08:56,845 --> 00:08:58,386
Look at these.

132
00:08:58,470 --> 00:09:02,261
Most people I know wear shoes like these
these days, so I bought a pair too.

133
00:09:02,511 --> 00:09:06,095
I walk around all day
taking care of patients and standing,

134
00:09:07,678 --> 00:09:10,220
but my feet don't hurt at all.
You should look into these.

135
00:09:10,986 --> 00:09:11,986
Really?

136
00:09:15,386 --> 00:09:17,011
- They do look comfortable.
- Yeah.

137
00:09:23,970 --> 00:09:25,803
So Sa Bin gave these to you?

138
00:09:25,886 --> 00:09:28,053
Yeah, for living expenses.

139
00:09:29,803 --> 00:09:32,793
For two people. Got it.

140
00:09:33,970 --> 00:09:35,595
It must be nice
getting living expenses again.

141
00:09:35,678 --> 00:09:38,136
Yeah. It made me feel married.

142
00:09:40,341 --> 00:09:43,095
It's a wife's privilege to make a home.

143
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:46,240
I guess you'd know, having done it before.

144
00:09:46,581 --> 00:09:47,928
I'm still figuring it out.

145
00:09:48,386 --> 00:09:50,892
That's why I told you not to do it.

146
00:09:51,394 --> 00:09:53,567
Experience makes all the difference.

147
00:09:54,136 --> 00:09:59,636
How hard must it be to teach
our young, immature Sa Bin how to live?

148
00:10:00,011 --> 00:10:03,528
Even giving him looks at breakfast
every morning doesn't seem to work.

149
00:10:03,761 --> 00:10:07,011
- Sun Kyung...
- Do you know how ridiculous it is?

150
00:10:07,303 --> 00:10:09,011
It's like a comedy show.

151
00:10:09,428 --> 00:10:11,420
That's enough. You're being harsh.

152
00:10:11,521 --> 00:10:12,761
That's enough, Sun Kyung.

153
00:10:12,803 --> 00:10:14,632
Fine. That's enough.

154
00:10:15,426 --> 00:10:18,761
This much money should smooth things over.

155
00:10:19,718 --> 00:10:23,095
Whenever I try to talk to you
like a friend, you act like this.

156
00:10:23,178 --> 00:10:24,833
How could I ever be your friend?

157
00:10:25,061 --> 00:10:27,112
We're on completely different levels.

158
00:10:27,261 --> 00:10:28,261
Family?

159
00:10:29,171 --> 00:10:32,386
Do you really think
you can become one of us?

160
00:10:33,886 --> 00:10:38,511
I doubt you'll keep playing
the devoted wife for long.

161
00:10:38,595 --> 00:10:40,772
Sa Bin, your brother-in-law,

162
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:43,220
isn't a fool who needs saving,
and I'm not here to rescue him.

163
00:10:43,345 --> 00:10:45,902
We love each other and live our lives
our own way.

164
00:10:46,024 --> 00:10:47,136
So stop judging us.

165
00:10:47,178 --> 00:10:48,220
Sister-in-law.

166
00:10:48,636 --> 00:10:52,136
"Sister-in-law" when it suits you.
Yes, Sister-in-law.

167
00:10:52,303 --> 00:10:55,231
I'm not used to living off others.

168
00:10:55,470 --> 00:10:57,075
But do you know...

169
00:10:57,396 --> 00:10:59,845
how good it feels to earn your own money?

170
00:11:01,053 --> 00:11:04,075
Don't be so narrow-minded.

171
00:11:04,350 --> 00:11:06,595
Open your mind, sister-in-law.

172
00:11:09,886 --> 00:11:11,011
That little...

173
00:11:15,974 --> 00:11:18,535
Hey, I'm still your elder sister-in-law.

174
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:21,641
Do you want me to hit you
with flowers again?

175
00:11:26,803 --> 00:11:28,194
I won't let you hit me again.

176
00:11:28,929 --> 00:11:30,854
Why do you hate me so much?

177
00:11:30,928 --> 00:11:32,553
At least tell me why.

178
00:11:32,595 --> 00:11:33,928
Do you really not know?

179
00:11:35,497 --> 00:11:39,892
As the lady of this house,
I've protected my family and its dignity.

180
00:11:39,928 --> 00:11:42,802
I sacrificed my youth to build this life.

181
00:11:42,871 --> 00:11:43,996
And who are you?

182
00:11:45,011 --> 00:11:47,190
You were abandoned
and drifting from place to place...

183
00:11:47,191 --> 00:11:48,852
until you got lucky and met Sa Bin...

184
00:11:48,854 --> 00:11:53,637
and moved into my home overnight.
How is that fair?

185
00:11:53,678 --> 00:11:55,428
- Sun Kyung.
- What have you ever done?

186
00:11:55,678 --> 00:11:57,986
Did you ever support him
or manage the building?

187
00:11:58,248 --> 00:12:00,053
You got it all without earning it.

188
00:12:01,011 --> 00:12:05,970
You didn't earn your happiness
or any of that money.

189
00:12:06,343 --> 00:12:11,051
I can't accept you as my sister-in-law.
It's too unfair.

190
00:12:11,053 --> 00:12:14,636
We've already settled this.
You still can't accept our marriage?

191
00:12:14,678 --> 00:12:15,678
Didn't you know that?

192
00:12:17,098 --> 00:12:20,724
You'll spend the rest of your life
living under my thumb.

193
00:12:21,428 --> 00:12:23,845
Is that why you wanted me here?

194
00:12:23,886 --> 00:12:25,970
Why else would I live with you?

195
00:12:36,178 --> 00:12:38,803
(Don't pick up)

196
00:12:39,595 --> 00:12:40,636
Yes, it's me.

197
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:45,832
Really? Okay. Bye.

198
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:57,780
Where are you going?

199
00:12:59,511 --> 00:13:01,095
It's not banh xeo. Eat before you work.

200
00:13:02,928 --> 00:13:05,720
- So she's your little sister now?
- Grow up.

201
00:13:05,970 --> 00:13:09,603
She's mad at you. If I were cold too,
would she stay here?

202
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:12,471
If she left, Mom would be uneasy,
and everyone would suffer.

203
00:13:13,273 --> 00:13:15,261
You'll never understand an eagle's mind.

204
00:13:15,345 --> 00:13:17,803
I'm just a sparrow. How would I know?

205
00:13:18,136 --> 00:13:20,053
- How long will you be gone?
- I'm not telling you.

206
00:13:22,053 --> 00:13:25,220
Mr. Shin asked me to help film birds.

207
00:13:25,261 --> 00:13:27,428
A documentary again. That must be nice.

208
00:13:27,470 --> 00:13:29,001
No shoot is easy.

209
00:13:30,043 --> 00:13:31,886
Still, I'm glad. It's familiar work.

210
00:13:34,053 --> 00:13:35,345
Aren't you going into business
with Ms. Song?

211
00:13:36,011 --> 00:13:38,178
Ji Ni and her mom said
you should take charge.

212
00:13:38,386 --> 00:13:40,761
Everyone's desperate to put me in charge.

213
00:13:40,928 --> 00:13:43,970
Why not? It's better to work for yourself
than for someone else.

214
00:13:44,011 --> 00:13:45,886
Seriously, I'll decide for myself.

215
00:13:47,303 --> 00:13:50,261
He's gone now. Why does it matter
who founded the company?

216
00:13:50,761 --> 00:13:52,279
Do well, and it'll be yours.

217
00:13:52,514 --> 00:13:54,136
It's 2026. Live in the present.

218
00:13:54,803 --> 00:13:57,178
It's bad enough I'm stuck in the past.

219
00:13:58,720 --> 00:13:59,720
Seung Hyun.

220
00:14:00,053 --> 00:14:01,572
I need to move on soon too.

221
00:14:02,693 --> 00:14:03,718
Remember?

222
00:14:04,636 --> 00:14:07,595
Mom used to call it "life-deaf."

223
00:14:07,678 --> 00:14:08,886
You mean Dad...

224
00:14:10,636 --> 00:14:12,011
That's what she called him.

225
00:14:12,053 --> 00:14:13,053
Yes.

226
00:14:13,759 --> 00:14:15,912
In the end, he failed us and left.

227
00:14:16,534 --> 00:14:17,805
Let's not become like him.

228
00:14:18,428 --> 00:14:20,553
At least Mom started over.

229
00:14:21,678 --> 00:14:25,470
Seung Hyun, you're becoming more of a nag
by the day.

230
00:14:45,189 --> 00:14:47,148
- Honey.
- You startled me.

231
00:14:48,095 --> 00:14:50,303
What's this all of a sudden?

232
00:14:50,761 --> 00:14:54,470
Stop saying your legs hurt. Try these on.

233
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:58,845
I asked you to get me an herbal tonic,
not buy me shoes.

234
00:14:59,010 --> 00:15:01,718
Besides, I only wear heels.

235
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:04,220
Just try them. Why keep wearing heels?

236
00:15:10,509 --> 00:15:13,384
They're comfortable.
It barely feels like I'm wearing shoes.

237
00:15:13,386 --> 00:15:16,178
Right? I should get Yeong Ju a pair too.

238
00:15:16,428 --> 00:15:18,636
She has a husband of her own.
Don't worry about her.

239
00:15:19,136 --> 00:15:24,220
Don't put her and me on the same level.
It's insulting.

240
00:15:24,261 --> 00:15:25,928
Okay.

241
00:15:28,636 --> 00:15:30,136
They're comfortable, right?

242
00:15:31,261 --> 00:15:32,303
They're so light.

243
00:15:34,803 --> 00:15:37,178
How about something like this?

244
00:15:37,428 --> 00:15:41,678
Something sparkly and glamorous,
or something bright pink.

245
00:15:41,803 --> 00:15:44,970
- Sparkly and pinky-pink.
- I love it.

246
00:15:45,038 --> 00:15:47,330
How can I wear something this nice
just around the house?

247
00:15:47,386 --> 00:15:50,026
You need to totally show her up.

248
00:15:50,027 --> 00:15:52,511
"You're not the only one with a husband.
I have one, too."

249
00:15:52,553 --> 00:15:56,345
You're a doctor's wife now.

250
00:15:57,095 --> 00:15:59,120
That sounds so strange.

251
00:15:59,315 --> 00:16:01,428
Anyway, okay. I'll buy this.

252
00:16:02,011 --> 00:16:03,345
- This one?
- Yes.

253
00:16:06,886 --> 00:16:08,928
Must be nice, using your husband's card.

254
00:16:08,970 --> 00:16:13,345
I'm the one who's jealous.
You were amazing that day.

255
00:16:13,886 --> 00:16:14,928
Really?

256
00:16:19,037 --> 00:16:21,954
I'm thankful for everything these days.

257
00:16:22,675 --> 00:16:27,384
It's amazing I'm living with Sa Bin,
and how things turned out between us.

258
00:16:29,148 --> 00:16:32,568
When I make the boys breakfast
each morning, I sometimes think...

259
00:16:32,570 --> 00:16:35,399
"Honey, I'm cooking here now..."

260
00:16:38,178 --> 00:16:39,678
That's not weird, is it?

261
00:16:39,928 --> 00:16:42,178
No. I have my own husband too.

262
00:16:44,345 --> 00:16:48,553
I'm glad you remarried.
You married a good man.

263
00:16:48,886 --> 00:16:50,345
That's how I feel too.

264
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:55,817
You need to tell Ji Ni soon
that you're working as a model.

265
00:16:55,818 --> 00:16:57,928
It'll hurt her more to find out later.

266
00:16:58,845 --> 00:17:00,386
I'll tell her once I'm more settled.

267
00:17:00,928 --> 00:17:05,095
Growing up, she only ever saw me playing
the cello on big stages,

268
00:17:05,803 --> 00:17:08,595
so she'll be shocked
if I suddenly tell her I'm modeling.

269
00:17:09,261 --> 00:17:11,468
I actually think you're impressive.

270
00:17:11,536 --> 00:17:14,011
You found a new path instead of giving up.

271
00:17:14,428 --> 00:17:15,831
It's not like I had a choice.

272
00:17:15,832 --> 00:17:18,345
What else can I do with this hand?

273
00:17:19,345 --> 00:17:20,720
But you're doing well.

274
00:17:22,261 --> 00:17:23,395
This is on you.

275
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:27,625
If you'd remarried sooner,
my husband would've had less heartache,

276
00:17:27,928 --> 00:17:29,761
so it's your fault I'm a widow.

277
00:17:30,595 --> 00:17:32,345
You always end up blaming me, right?

278
00:17:33,595 --> 00:17:37,513
He was sick and wanted ten years
of my life. You two...

279
00:17:37,850 --> 00:17:39,153
How can you be so much alike?

280
00:17:39,636 --> 00:17:41,261
I guess that's why we were married.

281
00:17:45,803 --> 00:17:46,803
(O Reum's Banh Xeo)

282
00:17:48,010 --> 00:17:50,435
(Banh Xeo, Original, Spicy,
O Reum's Banh Xeo)

283
00:18:06,476 --> 00:18:07,684
What's this?

284
00:18:07,732 --> 00:18:08,892
It's banh xeo.

285
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:10,970
It's a Vietnamese dish. Want to try some?

286
00:18:10,972 --> 00:18:13,085
That smells wonderful, sir.

287
00:18:13,136 --> 00:18:14,761
It's opening day. We're offering samples.

288
00:18:18,511 --> 00:18:21,553
Welcome! We're giving out samples today.
Have a taste.

289
00:18:25,550 --> 00:18:28,134
- Delicious, isn't it?
- It's really good!

290
00:18:28,136 --> 00:18:30,303
It's delicious. How much does it cost?

291
00:18:30,386 --> 00:18:31,386
Ten dollars.

292
00:18:31,527 --> 00:18:33,553
A regular serving is much bigger.

293
00:18:33,678 --> 00:18:37,011
There are so many vegetables in it
that you won't gain weight eating it.

294
00:18:37,761 --> 00:18:41,761
- You're really handsome, sir.
- You look like a celebrity.

295
00:18:41,845 --> 00:18:44,095
- You're so handsome.
- You're incredibly handsome.

296
00:18:44,803 --> 00:18:46,484
I didn't tell you, did I?

297
00:18:46,699 --> 00:18:48,803
We're actually shooting a TV show.

298
00:18:48,928 --> 00:18:50,136
This is all being filmed.

299
00:18:50,178 --> 00:18:51,375
- Where?
- Where?

300
00:18:51,757 --> 00:18:53,803
Just kidding. Got you!

301
00:18:55,220 --> 00:18:58,636
Please spread the word
so this place can get on TV.

302
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:03,053
Sir, you're really handsome.
Can we get a photo with you?

303
00:19:03,136 --> 00:19:05,303
Okay. Thank you.

304
00:19:06,386 --> 00:19:08,678
One, two, three.

305
00:19:14,470 --> 00:19:15,595
Are you going on a picnic?

306
00:19:16,470 --> 00:19:18,096
Didn't Ji Ni tell you?

307
00:19:18,638 --> 00:19:20,514
I got paid for my appearance.

308
00:19:20,515 --> 00:19:22,095
I'm dropping off snacks
at the publishing company.

309
00:19:22,136 --> 00:19:24,261
- Then I'll drive you in my car.
- Yes!

310
00:19:25,845 --> 00:19:29,011
Nothing's happened, right?
No one's come to harass you or anything?

311
00:19:29,053 --> 00:19:30,095
Nothing like that.

312
00:19:31,178 --> 00:19:33,430
- I just got back from a blind date.
- Really?

313
00:19:33,511 --> 00:19:34,970
The rumors will die down soon.

314
00:19:35,636 --> 00:19:37,678
You're really doing your best.

315
00:19:38,428 --> 00:19:40,636
I heard Ji Ni's dating Tae O too.

316
00:19:41,511 --> 00:19:43,428
- What?
- You didn't know?

317
00:19:44,303 --> 00:19:47,261
Well, I guess it would be awkward
to tell you.

318
00:19:48,053 --> 00:19:51,136
Do Do Hee has really shaken things up.

319
00:19:51,886 --> 00:19:54,553
I knew they hung out together,
but I didn't know they were dating.

320
00:19:54,595 --> 00:19:57,078
I think Tae O's liked her for a long time.

321
00:19:57,122 --> 00:19:59,889
- Really?
- It was pretty obvious.

322
00:19:59,890 --> 00:20:01,354
You didn't notice that either?

323
00:20:03,761 --> 00:20:05,819
Want me to buy drinks tonight?

324
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:10,345
I've barely had a drink since filming,
so I'm really craving one.

325
00:20:10,886 --> 00:20:12,419
- Just the two of us?
- If you get your picture taken with me,

326
00:20:12,434 --> 00:20:13,832
isn't that a good thing right now?

327
00:20:16,347 --> 00:20:17,347
Drinks?

328
00:20:17,431 --> 00:20:19,928
Ji Hu went on a blind date,
and you're going on a date.

329
00:20:20,095 --> 00:20:22,595
I'm the only one making money,
so I'll buy the drinks.

330
00:20:22,636 --> 00:20:26,402
- A blind date?
- Yeah. His mom told him to go on one.

331
00:20:26,490 --> 00:20:28,948
He's just desperate
to get away from Do Hee.

332
00:20:29,761 --> 00:20:33,511
You saw his face. He looked miserable.

333
00:20:38,136 --> 00:20:39,345
A home shopping show?

334
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:43,845
I sent this to every home shopping
production company.

335
00:20:44,428 --> 00:20:49,053
Of course I'm interested.
How much does it pay?

336
00:20:49,886 --> 00:20:53,095
- Five thousand dollars?
- No.

337
00:20:53,303 --> 00:20:55,998
You're asking for too much
right off the bat. Five hundred.

338
00:20:56,470 --> 00:20:57,636
Five hundred?

339
00:20:58,261 --> 00:21:01,970
What? At this rate,
when will I ever afford a house?

340
00:21:03,097 --> 00:21:04,597
So what's the split?

341
00:21:04,803 --> 00:21:07,678
- Sixty, forty?
- That's too much.

342
00:21:08,720 --> 00:21:11,636
Then 65, 35?

343
00:21:12,386 --> 00:21:14,720
I need to make something too.
I have to live alone when I'm old.

344
00:21:15,386 --> 00:21:16,386
Fine.

345
00:21:16,603 --> 00:21:20,011
If you have nowhere to go when you're old,
come live with me. I'll give you a room.

346
00:21:20,178 --> 00:21:22,470
Really? I will. I'm holding you to that.

347
00:21:22,886 --> 00:21:25,428
Fine. Come on over.

348
00:21:35,345 --> 00:21:38,303
You smell like cooking oil.
Did you sell a lot today?

349
00:21:40,970 --> 00:21:43,204
Say something. Does it cost you to talk?

350
00:21:43,970 --> 00:21:44,970
What do you want me to say?

351
00:21:44,996 --> 00:21:47,945
What kind of cake do you like?
Carrot, strawberry, mocha, what?

352
00:21:48,001 --> 00:21:49,428
Your birthday's in a few days.

353
00:21:49,470 --> 00:21:50,511
Never mind.

354
00:21:51,470 --> 00:21:53,053
Then I'll get you a mustard cake.

355
00:21:54,553 --> 00:21:55,595
Chocolate.

356
00:21:58,970 --> 00:22:01,595
Chocolate? Since when has he had
such a sweet tooth?

357
00:22:17,136 --> 00:22:18,178
Guess who?

358
00:22:20,511 --> 00:22:22,470
I surrender.

359
00:22:22,636 --> 00:22:25,377
Director, I thought my arm would fall off.

360
00:22:25,378 --> 00:22:28,761
Look. It almost did.
What am I going to do?

361
00:22:31,261 --> 00:22:32,720
Did you put a tracker on me?

362
00:22:33,331 --> 00:22:35,807
How did you know? Just kidding.

363
00:22:35,895 --> 00:22:37,220
Ms. Song told me.

364
00:22:37,761 --> 00:22:39,095
Don't get in the way. Go.

365
00:22:39,428 --> 00:22:41,465
Director, wait.

366
00:22:41,620 --> 00:22:44,159
Now that the show's over,
can I call you Seung Woo?

367
00:22:44,803 --> 00:22:48,095
Seung Woo, how long have you been at this?
Aren't you bored?

368
00:22:48,220 --> 00:22:49,802
No, I'm not bored.

369
00:22:50,136 --> 00:22:51,577
You really like filming that much?

370
00:22:51,906 --> 00:22:54,845
Your eyes change behind the camera.
It's kind of cool.

371
00:22:59,303 --> 00:23:02,261
I said you're cool.
When someone compliments you, say it back.

372
00:23:02,470 --> 00:23:05,803
You're pretty cool too.
You've been going crazy for 24 hours.

373
00:23:07,970 --> 00:23:10,678
What the heck? Why is an insult so funny?

374
00:23:11,386 --> 00:23:13,636
You have that tough-but-sweet charm.

375
00:23:15,636 --> 00:23:17,345
My legs hurt. Give me a chair.

376
00:23:29,595 --> 00:23:30,678
Why are you giving me a drink?

377
00:23:31,136 --> 00:23:32,677
Have a drink with me.

378
00:23:32,931 --> 00:23:35,875
For the first time in decades,
my mom praised me today.

379
00:23:36,970 --> 00:23:40,261
My follower count went up,
and I got my revenge on Ji Hu.

380
00:23:41,636 --> 00:23:44,095
It's the first time
my mom has ever praised me.

381
00:23:45,928 --> 00:23:48,294
People around her say
she raised her daughter well.

382
00:23:48,989 --> 00:23:50,678
Is this what happiness feels like?

383
00:23:53,136 --> 00:23:55,232
It felt so good,

384
00:23:57,580 --> 00:23:59,428
but it also felt so empty.

385
00:24:00,845 --> 00:24:04,386
Why did I spend so long
desperately wanting something so small?

386
00:24:07,053 --> 00:24:08,288
You don't know what that's like, right?

387
00:24:09,189 --> 00:24:10,720
You grew up hearing only praise, right?

388
00:24:10,803 --> 00:24:13,553
My mom worries about me too,
afraid I might fall.

389
00:24:14,636 --> 00:24:17,095
Don't people get over being afraid
of falling before elementary school?

390
00:24:21,386 --> 00:24:22,470
I got hurt when I was little.

391
00:24:26,178 --> 00:24:29,595
- You're not surprised?
- What? You don't need my pity.

392
00:24:33,294 --> 00:24:36,253
Aren't you supposed to give up your seat
for the injured?

393
00:24:36,428 --> 00:24:39,511
My legs hurt from wearing heels too.
Let's take turns sitting.

394
00:24:55,720 --> 00:24:57,178
You smiled.

395
00:25:02,261 --> 00:25:05,761
What are you filming?
That red ball over there?

396
00:25:09,136 --> 00:25:10,803
Why? Let's film it together.

397
00:25:15,845 --> 00:25:16,928
Cheers!

398
00:25:22,261 --> 00:25:24,845
Do you think this will actually help?

399
00:25:25,095 --> 00:25:27,386
People there were already taking notice.

400
00:25:27,678 --> 00:25:29,249
Someone will probably post it online.

401
00:25:29,344 --> 00:25:31,386
And even if it doesn't work, so what?

402
00:25:32,053 --> 00:25:33,774
I'm having fun hanging out with you.

403
00:25:34,678 --> 00:25:35,720
Me too.

404
00:25:36,886 --> 00:25:39,052
We've known each other for a long time,

405
00:25:39,454 --> 00:25:42,428
but I actually don't know much about you.

406
00:25:43,470 --> 00:25:44,693
There's not much to know about me.

407
00:25:45,021 --> 00:25:46,697
I'm just like everyone else.

408
00:25:47,386 --> 00:25:49,345
Maybe I'm different, though.

409
00:25:50,101 --> 00:25:51,383
But that's all in the past.

410
00:25:51,504 --> 00:25:53,309
Why push love away
when it wasn't even your fault?

411
00:25:54,428 --> 00:25:56,261
Aren't you too hung up on the past?

412
00:25:57,053 --> 00:26:00,553
- Hey, Ji Ni. Open up!
- Okay.

413
00:26:07,662 --> 00:26:09,746
But even the people who say that,

414
00:26:10,428 --> 00:26:16,136
when I'm doing fine, tell me I'm too
comfortable and that I feel no guilt.

415
00:26:16,345 --> 00:26:19,553
Sorry. I didn't think before I spoke.

416
00:26:21,677 --> 00:26:23,205
But I've learned a lot too.

417
00:26:23,612 --> 00:26:25,220
I've learned that love is scary.

418
00:26:25,345 --> 00:26:27,632
It can make you throw caution aside...

419
00:26:28,001 --> 00:26:30,886
and completely take over your life.

420
00:26:31,136 --> 00:26:33,220
Hey, that's a little dramatic.

421
00:26:34,095 --> 00:26:38,227
Either way, I can't control love.

422
00:26:38,407 --> 00:26:39,470
I'll never fall in love.

423
00:26:39,511 --> 00:26:41,417
That's a pretty strong wall.

424
00:26:42,339 --> 00:26:44,970
This date feels
more like a philosophy class.

425
00:26:45,553 --> 00:26:48,928
- Ji Ni, me too. Feed me.
- Open up!

426
00:26:54,636 --> 00:26:56,636
- Pretending to date?
- Yes.

427
00:26:56,761 --> 00:26:58,748
That's why we're going on a date today.

428
00:26:59,129 --> 00:27:01,618
"Someone, please post it online."

429
00:27:02,428 --> 00:27:05,095
Anyway, we're all really suffering
because of Do Hee.

430
00:27:11,307 --> 00:27:13,057
Do you like Ji Ni?

431
00:27:14,886 --> 00:27:16,317
I shouldn't like her.

432
00:27:16,679 --> 00:27:18,314
She's the one who says
she'll never fall in love.

433
00:27:19,386 --> 00:27:21,720
Is there someone you like right now?

434
00:27:22,178 --> 00:27:24,136
- Why?
- Just curious.

435
00:27:25,053 --> 00:27:26,928
Are you going to see that person
from your blind date again?

436
00:27:26,970 --> 00:27:28,053
I'm not sure.

437
00:27:28,803 --> 00:27:33,257
Right now, I can't face Ji Ni, Tae O,
the people at the publishing company,

438
00:27:33,659 --> 00:27:34,886
or my parents.

439
00:27:35,761 --> 00:27:37,553
Because all this happened because of me.

440
00:27:37,595 --> 00:27:39,511
Why is it your fault, Ji Hu?

441
00:27:39,761 --> 00:27:40,886
It is my fault.

442
00:27:43,261 --> 00:27:45,136
What about you, Jung A?
Is there someone you like?

443
00:27:47,178 --> 00:27:50,470
- There is.
- Who? Someone I know?

444
00:27:52,720 --> 00:27:56,678
Maybe. Maybe not.

445
00:28:29,886 --> 00:28:33,136
(Family Register)

446
00:28:33,178 --> 00:28:37,178
We were drinking when he got so drunk
that I couldn't do anything.

447
00:28:37,220 --> 00:28:38,761
Ji Ni has a boyfriend?

448
00:28:38,803 --> 00:28:40,220
Isn't this going to backfire on Do Hee?

449
00:28:40,261 --> 00:28:42,595
I'm sorry, but I'd like you to leave.

450
00:28:42,636 --> 00:28:44,595
I've never gotten a bouquet
of purple flowers before.

451
00:28:44,636 --> 00:28:46,635
I guess you're single now.
I'll call you Se Ri.

452
00:28:46,636 --> 00:28:47,635
Sure. I like it.

453
00:28:47,636 --> 00:28:49,629
I may not say it, but I'm rooting for you.

454
00:28:49,630 --> 00:28:51,428
You must be having a hard time too,
just like me.

455
00:28:51,470 --> 00:28:53,928
They say someone saw
the motorcycle that hit Seung Woo.

456
00:28:54,410 --> 00:28:56,410
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
